      "predicate": "doctrinal_mapping",
      "object_id": null,
      "value": "Atri maps name/form to Śakti/asat, immortal self to Solar/sat, their unity to Viṣṇu/sadasat, distinct fourth/neti/nirmoha/independence to Śiva, and fourfold union to māyā-Svānanda Gaṇeśa. Karma yoga joins acts; knowledge yoga joins knowledge; their nonduality gives sama/ānanda; freely adopting/rejecting these is independent sahaja. Svānanda union joins worlds/Brahmans in nondifference; ayoga excludes union/entry and māyā, described as nirvṛtti. He distinguishes Svānanda-residing Gaṇeśa from mere Svānanda identity, play/union from playless yoga; dissolution of both saṃyoga/ayoga is Gaṇeśa’s peace/full yoga, where with/without māyā distinction is delusion. Terms remain this teacher’s doctrinal maps, not cross-school equivalences.",
